{"type":"message","id":"000dbb49","parentId":"23c9756e","timestamp":"2026-04-01T23:04:37.462Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_bNJvD1mGt6MlINQpheveJvDA|fc_092a77d0e028a4910169cda482f2a88191b7dbd3d1c6852acc","toolName":"web_search","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"query\": \"site:github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues \\\"2026.4.1\\\" \\\"regression\\\" openclaw\",\n  \"provider\": \"tavily\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 2425,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"tavily\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"74897f996f72e893\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n[Bug]:Configuration regression causing startup dead-lock · Issue #9390 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"74897f996f72e893\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/9390\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d5feef738d8f55fe\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTitle: [Bug]:Configuration regression causing startup dead-lock · Issue #9390 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # [Bug]:Configuration regression causing startup dead-lock #9390. [[Bug]:Configuration regression causing startup dead-lock](#top)#9390. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't workingstaleMarked as stale due to inactivityMarked as stale due to inactivity. ## Description. opened on Feb 5, 2026. ## Summary. On macOS, the gateway cannot start at all in OpenClaw 2026.1.30. The gateway enforces a mandatory `gateway.mode` check, but there is **no functional way to set this value**:. * `--allow-unconfigured` flag is ignored. As a result, the gateway always exits during startup validation and the TUI is completely unusable. This is a release-blocking regression. ## Steps to reproduce. 1. Install OpenClaw 2026.1.30 on macOS. 3. Observe that the gateway exits immediately with:Gateway start blocked: set gateway.mode=local (current: unset) or pass --allow-unconfigured. 4.(Optional) Try all documented/indicated configuration methods:. • Create ~/.config/openclaw/config.json5 with{. • Run：OPENCLAW\\\\_GATEWAY\\\\_MODE=local openclaw gateway run. Run：openclaw gateway run --allow-unconfigured openclaw gateway --allow-unconfigured run. 4. Observe that the gateway is still blocked in all cases. 5. Observe that TUI cannot connect because the gateway never starts. At least one of the following should work:. • gateway.mode can be set via config file. • gateway.mode can be set via environment variable. The gateway should start and remain running, allowing openclaw tui to connect successfully. • gateway.mode always remains unset. • All configuration methods (config file, env var, CLI flag) are ignored. • Gateway exits during startup validation. • TUI always shows gateway disconnected: closed | idle. • Clawdbot version: OpenClaw 2026.1.30 (76b5208). • Install method: prebuilt binary / Homebrew. Gateway start blocked: set gateway.mode=local (current: unset) or pass --allow-unconfigured. openclaw tui - ws://127.0.0.1:18789 - agent main - session main. agent main | session main | unknown | tokens ? ## Metadata. ## Metadata. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d5feef738d8f55fe\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.9999907\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d9b34991742ebfe4\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n[Bug]: Regression: All channel plugins disabled in v2026.2.22 (works in 2026.2.19) · Issue #24395 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d9b34991742ebfe4\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/24395\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1832d385be6ea542\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTitle: [Bug]: Regression: All channel plugins disabled in v2026.2.22 (works in 2026.2.19) · Issue #24395 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n# [Bug]: Regression: All channel plugins disabled in v2026.2.22 (works in 2026.2.19) #24395. [[Bug]: Regression: All channel plugins disabled in v2026.2.22 (works in 2026.2.19)](#top)#24395. All channel plugins remain `disabled` despite correct configuration. set \\\"YOUR_TOKEN\\\" \\\" \\\" # Channels section is EMPTY # ### Steps to reproduce #'s the clean copy-paste version for **\\\"Steps to Reproduce\\\"**: ' ```markdown ## Steps to Reproduce ### 1. Install broken version ```bashnpm install -g openclaw@2026.2.22. **Output:** `│ telegram │ disabled │ stock:telegram/index.ts │`. npm install -g openclaw@2026.2.19 openclaw gateway restart openclaw status. **Output:** `│ Telegram │ ON │ OK │ token config (...) · accounts 1/1 │` ✅. --- **Paste that into the GitHub issue under \\\"Steps to Reproduce\\\"** — it's deterministic and shows the version regression clearly. ### Expected behavior **Expected Behavior:** ```markdown ## Expected Behavior When `channels.telegram.enabled: true` is set and a valid `botToken` is configured: 1. **Plugin loads:** Telegram plugin status shows `loaded` (not `disabled`) 2. **Gateway initializes:** Startup logs show Telegram bot starting 3. **Status shows channel:** `openclaw status` displays:. 4. **Bot responds:** Messages sent to the Telegram bot are received by OpenClaw This works correctly in **v2026.2.19** and earlier versions. openclaw plugins list | grep telegram. │ telegram │ disabled │ stock:telegram/index.ts │ 2026.2.22 │. 2. **No channel initialization:** Gateway startup logs show NO Telegram initialization:. # No telegram, grammy, or channel plugin logs appear. 3. **Empty channels section:** `openclaw status` shows:. 4. **All channel plugins affected:** Not just Telegram — Discord, Slack, Signal, WhatsApp, etc. access '/.../openclaw/extensions/stock/telegram/index.ts'. ## Actual Behavior Actual Behavior ` disabled ` ` openclaw status ` `extensions/stock/telegram/index.ts `. ### OpenClaw version. **OpenClaw Version:** 2026.2.22 **Last Working Version:** 2026.2.19. ** &** ## Environment # | | | | | | |**** | | |**** | | |**** | | |**** |`npm install -g openclaw` ` ` | ## Logs #### Plugin Discovery (Broken) #### Plugin List Output (Broken - v2026.2.22) #### Plugin List Output (Working - v2026.2.19) # ### Key Error # read'/Users/admin/.nvm/versions/node/v24.13.1/lib/node_modules/openclaw/extensions/stock/telegram/index.ts' ' '### Gateway Startup (No Channel Initialization) # \\\"subsystem\\\" \\\" \\\"\\\"hooks:loader\\\" \\\" \\\"> \\\"subsystem\\\" \\\" \\\"\\\"gateway/heartbeat\\\" \\\" \\\" \\\"subsystem\\\" \\\" \\\"\\\"gateway/health-monitor\\\" \\\" \\\"**** `telegram` ` ` `grammy` ` `**** else for ?\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1832d385be6ea542\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.9999654\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"97b453700458f7f5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCLI status/health commands hang after output (regression?) · Issue #11843 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"97b453700458f7f5\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/11843\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3210675c6624d94d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTitle: CLI status/health commands hang after output (regression?) · Issue #11843 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # CLI status/health commands hang after output (regression?) #11843. CLI status/health commands hang after output (regression?)#11843. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't workingstaleMarked as stale due to inactivityMarked as stale due to inactivity. ## Description. opened on Feb 8, 2026. ### Bug. `openclaw` CLI commands (e.g. `openclaw gateway status --json`, `openclaw browser status`) sometimes **hang** and do not return to the shell prompt. This appears to be new/regression after recent update (2026.2.6-3). The CLI prints plugin init logs and stays running even for status/health commands. ### Expected. Status/health commands should exit after printing JSON. ### Actual. Process stays running; requires manual kill (`Ctrl+C` doesn’t always exit). `timeout` sometimes also does not terminate. ### Steps to reproduce. ### Output (trimmed). [plugins] [unbrowse] Auto-discover: 3 existing skills loaded [plugins] [token-refresh] Scheduler started (checking every 1min) [plugins] [unbrowse] Auto-discovery hook active [plugins] [unbrowse] Plugin registered (16 tools, auto-discover) { ... ### Environment. * OpenClaw: 2026.2.6-3. ### Notes. Seems like CLI is starting full runtime/plugins and not exiting for status commands. Possibly a regression in CLI lifecycle or plugin init. ## Metadata. ## Metadata. ### Labels. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't workingstaleMarked as stale due to inactivityMarked as stale due to inactivity. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3210675c6624d94d\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.9999615\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTE