auto-update run). 2. Wait for update to complete. 3. Try to open the gateway dashboard → offline. 4. Gateway does not restart itself. ## Expected Behavior. Gateway restarts automatically after an update, as it did before 2026.3.8. ## Actual Behavior. ## Additional Notes. * `openclaw gateway restart` via the exec tool also exhibits this issue (kills gateway, doesn't restart it). * Workaround: manually run the launchctl command above. ## Metadata. ## Metadata. ### Assignees. ### Fields. No fields configured for issues without a type. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d6b6c1a346b296dd\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.9998969\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"35f4d7df44271b8d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n[Bug]: Token usage shows as 'unknown' in 2026.3.7 (regression from 3.2) · Issue #39620 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"35f4d7df44271b8d\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/39773/linked_closing_reference?reference_location=REPO_ISSUES_INDEX\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9a5e91a5cfbe014f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nToken usage information displays as \\\"unknown\\\" in session\\\\_status and openclaw sessions output after upgrading to OpenClaw 2026.3.7. usage payloads, so session history/status no longer regress to unknown token utilization for otherwise successful runs.\\\" This suggests a fix was attempted, but it appears to have introduced or not fully resolved the issue. Regression Testing2026.3.2: Token usage displays correctly2026.3.7: Token usage shows as \\\"unknown\\\" Impact Cannot monitor API costs during sessions Cannot track context window usage Difficult to manage token budget for long conversations WorkaroundDowngrade to OpenClaw 2026.3.2: pnpm remove -g openclawpnpm install -g openclaw@2026.3.2 Possible CausesContextEngine plugin interface changes in 3.7 may have broken usage reportingkimi-k2.5 model usage parsing may have regressed Status display formatting may not be reading usage data correctly despite API success Requested FixRestore token usage display in session_status and openclaw sessions output for 2026.3.7+. Token usage information displays as \\\"unknown\\\" in session\\\\_status and openclaw sessions output after upgrading to OpenClaw 2026.3.7. Token usage information displays as \\\"unknown\\\" in session\\\\_status and openclaw sessions output after upgrading to OpenClaw 2026.3.7.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9a5e91a5cfbe014f\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.99985576\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1022ee1d3d270132\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nUser-installed plugins cannot resolve `openclaw/plugin-sdk` module path (regression in 3.23) · Issue #53403 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1022ee1d3d270132\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/53403\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"65c784e8b6d4d1fe\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTitle: User-installed plugins cannot resolve `openclaw/plugin-sdk` module path (regression in 3.23) · Issue #53403 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\n# Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. You signed out in another tab or window. You switched accounts on another tab or window. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # User-installed plugins cannot resolve `openclaw/plugin-sdk` module path (regression in 3.23) #53403. User-installed plugins cannot resolve `openclaw/plugin-sdk` module path (regression in 3.23)#53403. * OpenClaw 3.23 (ccfeecb) and 3.23-1. * macOS 15.7.4 x64. * Plugin: `@tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin` 1.0.2 / 1.0.3. * Plugin install path: `~/.openclaw/extensions/openclaw-weixin/`. 1. Install OpenClaw 3.23. 2. Install any user plugin that imports from `openclaw/plugin-sdk` (e.g. 3. 3. Start or restart the gateway 4. Plugin fails to load: `Error: Cannot find module 'openclaw/plugin-sdk'`. Bundled plugins (feishu, etc.) work fine — the issue only affects user-installed plugins in `~/.openclaw/extensions/`. ## Root Cause. In `pi-embedded-CwMQzdKD.js`, `loadOpenClawPlugins()` calls `buildPluginLoaderAliasMap(modulePath)` where `modulePath` is the plugin file path (e.g. `~/.openclaw/extensions/openclaw-weixin/index.ts`). The jiti-based loader uses this to build an alias map for `openclaw/plugin-sdk*` imports. The alias map builder has two resolution paths:. Finds `root-alias.cjs` by walking **up to 6 levels** from the plugin directory. For `~/.openclaw/extensions/openclaw-weixin/`:. 1. ~/.openclaw/extensions/openclaw-weixin/ 2. Never reaches `/usr/local/lib/node_modules/openclaw/` → returns `null`. Calls `resolveLoaderPluginSdkPackageRoot()` → `resolveOpenClawPackageRootSync()` starting from plugin dirname, then `findNearestPluginSdkPackageRoot()` (max 12 levels). Same problem — cannot reach the OpenClaw package root from `~/.openclaw/extensions/`. ### Why it worked in 3.13. In 3.13, the alias for `openclaw/plugin-sdk` (main entry only) used a different resolution strategy that could locate the OpenClaw package. In 3.23, both main entry and subpath resolution fail for user-installed plugins. Bundled plugins work because they are located at `/usr/local/lib/node_modules/openclaw/dist/extensions/` — inside the same package tree. 1. **Search the OpenClaw executable's location** as a candidate root in `resolveLoaderPluginSdkPackageRoot()`. 2. **Set `NODE_PATH`** to include the OpenClaw package parent in the gateway LaunchAgent. 3. **Add a config option** like `plugins.sdkPath` pointing to the OpenClaw installation directory. 4. **Extend the directory walk limit** or use `require.resolve()` to find the OpenClaw package from the gateway process itself. cc @X\\\\_Corperation (who reported the same issue in the community). ### Fields. No fields configured for issues without a type. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"65c784e8b6d4d1fe\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.99985456\n    }\n  ]\n}"}],"details":{"query":"site:github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues \"2026.4.1\" \"regression\" openclaw","provider":"tavily","count":10,"tookMs":2425,"externalContent":{"untrusted":true,"source":"web_search","provider":"tavily","wrapped":true},"results":[{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"74897f996f72e893\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]:Configuration regression causing startup dead-lock · Issue #9390 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"74897f996f72e893\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/9390","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d5feef738d8f55fe\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTitle: [Bug]:Configuration regression causing startup dead-lock · Issue #9390 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # [Bug]:Configuration regression causing startup dead-lock #9390. [[Bug]:Configuration regression causing startup dead-lock](#top)#9390. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't workingstaleMarked as stale due to inactivityMarked as stale due to inactivity. ## Description. opened on Feb 5, 2026. ## Summary. On macOS, the gateway cannot start at all in OpenClaw 2026.1.30. The gateway enforces a mandatory `gateway.mode` check, but there is **no functional way to set this value**:. * `--allow-unconfigured` flag is ignored. As a result, the gateway always exits during startup validation and the TUI is completely unusable. This is a release-blocking regression. ## Steps to reproduce. 1. Install OpenClaw 2026.1.30 on macOS. 3. Observe that the gateway exits immediately with:Gateway start blocked: set gateway.mode=local (current: unset) or pass --allow-unconfigured. 4.(Optional) Try all documented/indicated configuration methods:. • Create ~/.config/openclaw/config.json5 with{. • Run：OPENCLAW\\_GATEWAY\\_MODE=local openclaw gateway run. Run：openclaw gateway run --allow-unconfigured openclaw gateway --allow-unconfigured run. 4. Observe that the gateway is still blocked in all cases. 5. Observe that TUI cannot connect because the gateway never starts. At least one of the following should work:. • gateway.mode can be set via config file. • gateway.mode can be set via environment variable. The gateway should start and remain running, allowing openclaw tui to connect successfully. • gateway.mode always remains unset. • All configuration methods (config file, env var, CLI flag) are ignored. • Gateway exits during startup validation. • TUI always shows gateway disconnected: closed | idle. • Clawdbot version: OpenClaw 2026.1.30 (76b5208). • Install method: prebuilt binary / Homebrew. Gateway start blocked: set gateway.mode=local (current: unset) or pass --allow-unconfigured. openclaw tui - ws://127.0.0.1:18789 - agent main - session main. agent main | session main | unknown | tokens ? ## Metadata. ## Metadata. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d5feef738d8f55fe\">>>","score":0.9999907},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d9b34991742ebfe4\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: Regression: All channel plugins disabled in v2026.2.22 (works in 2026.2.19) · Issue #24395 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d9b34991742ebfe4\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/24395","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1832d385be6ea542\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTitle: [Bug]: Regression: All channel plugins disabled in v2026.2.22 (works in 2026.2.19) · Issue #24395 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n# [Bug]: Regression: All channel plugins disabled in v2026.2.22 (works in 2026.2.19) #24395. [[Bug]: Regression: All channel plugins disabled in v2026.2.22 (works in 2026.2.19)](#top)#24395. All channel plugins remain `disabled` despite correct configuration. set \"YOUR_TOKEN\" \" \" # Channels section is EMPTY # ### Steps to reproduce #'s the clean copy-paste version for **\"Steps to Reproduce\"**: ' ```markdown ## Steps to Reproduce ### 1. Install broken version ```bashnpm install -g openclaw@2026.2.22. **Output:** `│ telegram │ disabled │ stock:telegram/index.ts │`. npm install -g openclaw@2026.2.19 openclaw gateway restart openclaw status. **Output:** `│ Telegram │ ON │ OK │ token config (...) · accounts 1/1 │` ✅. --- **Paste that into the GitHub issue under \"Steps to Reproduce\"** — it's deterministic and shows the version regression clearly. ### Expected behavior **Expected Behavior:** ```markdown ## Expected Behavior When `channels.telegram.enabled: true` is set and a valid `botToken` is configured: 1. **Plugin loads:** Telegram plugin status shows `loaded` (not `disabled`) 2. **Gateway initializes:** Startup logs show Telegram bot starting 3. **Status shows channel:** `openclaw status` displays:. 4. **Bot responds:** Messages sent to the Telegram bot are received by OpenClaw This works correctly in **v2026.2.19** and earlier versions. openclaw plugins list | grep telegram. │ telegram │ disabled │ stock:telegram/index.ts │ 2026.2.22 │. 2. **No channel initialization:** Gateway startup logs show NO Telegram initialization:. # No telegram, grammy, or channel plugin logs appear. 3. **Empty channels section:** `openclaw status` shows:. 4. **All channel plugins affected:** Not just Telegram — Discord, Slack, Signal, WhatsApp, etc. access '/.../openclaw/extensions/stock/telegram/index.ts'. ## Actual Behavior Actual Behavior ` disabled ` ` openclaw status ` `extensions/stock/telegram/index.ts `. ### OpenClaw version. **OpenClaw Version:** 2026.2.22 **Last Working Version:** 2026.2.19. ** &** ## Environment # | | | | | | |**** | | |**** | | |**** | | |**** |`npm install -g openclaw` ` ` | ## Logs #### Plugin Discovery (Broken) #### Plugin List Output (Broken - v2026.2.22) #### Plugin List Output (Working - v2026.2.19) # ### Key Error # read'/Users/admin/.nvm/versions/node/v24.13.1/lib/node_modules/openclaw/extensions/stock/telegram/index.ts' ' '### Gateway Startup (No Channel Initialization) # \"subsystem\" \" \"\"hooks:loader\" \" \"> \"subsystem\" \" \"\"gateway/heartbeat\" \" \" \"subsystem\" \" \"\"gateway/health-monitor\" \" \"**** `telegram` ` ` `grammy` ` `**** else for ?\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1832d385be6ea542\">>>","score":0.9999654},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"97b453700458f7f5\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nCLI status/health commands hang after output (regression?) · Issue #11843 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"97b453700458f7f5\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/11843","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3210675c6624d94d\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTitle: CLI status/health commands hang after output (regression?) · Issue #11843 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # CLI status/health commands hang after output (regression?) #11843. CLI status/health commands hang after output (regression?)#11843. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't workingstaleMarked as stale due to inactivityMarked as stale due to inactivity. ## Description. opened on Feb 8, 2026. ### Bug. `openclaw` CLI commands (e.g. `openclaw gateway status --json`, `openclaw browser status`) sometimes **hang** and do not return to the shell prompt. This appears to be new/regression after recent update (2026.2.6-3). The CLI prints plugin init logs and stays running even for status/health commands. ### Expected. Status/health commands should exit after printing JSON. ### Actual. Process stays running; requires manual kill (`Ctrl+C` doesn’t always exit). `timeout` sometimes also does not terminate. ### Steps to reproduce. ### Output (trimmed). [plugins] [unbrowse] Auto-discover: 3 existing skills loaded [plugins] [token-refresh] Scheduler started (checking every 1min) [plugins] [unbrowse] Auto-discovery hook active [plugins] [unbrowse] Plugin registered (16 tools, auto-discover) { ... ### Environment. * OpenClaw: 2026.2.6-3. ### Notes. Seems like CLI is starting full runtime/plugins and not exiting for status commands. Possibly a regression in CLI lifecycle or plugin init. ## Metadata. ## Metadata. ### Labels. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't workingstaleMarked as stale due to inactivityMarked as stale due to inactivity. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3210675c6624d94d\">>>","score":0.9999615},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8507aacbdbba4aa9\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Regression Bug]: OpenClaw browser profile (openclaw mode) fails to stay connected · Issue #30570 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8507aacbdbba4aa9\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/30570","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"43cbb6fcda6dfe7f\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTitle: [Regression Bug]: OpenClaw browser profile (openclaw mode) fails to stay connected · Issue #30570 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # [Regression Bug]: OpenClaw browser profile (openclaw mode) fails to stay connected #30570. [[Regression Bug]: OpenClaw browser profile (openclaw mode) fails to stay connected](#top)#30570. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't workingregressionBehavior that previously worked and now failsBehavior that previously worked and now fails. ## Description. opened on Mar 1, 2026. ### Summary. Browser control service starts but immediately disconnects in openclaw profile mode. ### Last known good version. 2026.2.22 or earlier. ### First known bad version. ### Regression window and trigger. Started after upgrading from 2026.2.22 to 2026.2.26; no config changes. Same version also has Telegram media download bug (#24854). ### Steps to reproduce. 1. Create new browser profile: `openclaw browser create-profile --name test --driver openclaw`. 2. Start the browser: `browser action=start profile=test`. 3. Service starts (logs show \"Browser control service ready\"). 4. But tool call times out - service immediately disconnects. ### Expected behavior. Browser should stay connected and be usable after starting. The service should remain active. ### Actual behavior. Logs show \"Browser control service ready (profiles=N)\" but tool call fails with timeout error: \"Can't reach the OpenClaw browser control service (timed out after 15000ms)\". Works fine with \"chrome\" (Relay) profile mode. ### Operating system. ### Install method. ### Logs, screenshots, and evidence. ### Impact and severity. Affected: Users who need browser automation in openclaw profile mode. Severity: High (blocks browser functionality). Consequence: Cannot use browser tool with openclaw profile, must use chrome/relay mode as workaround. ### Additional information. ## Metadata. ## Metadata. ### Labels. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't workingregressionBehavior that previously worked and now failsBehavior that previously worked and now fails. ### Fields. No fields configured for issues without a type. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"43cbb6fcda6dfe7f\">>>","score":0.99995315},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"feee315ff608b6fa\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: OpenClaw 2026.3.8 regression: empty agent payloads + websocket 1006 closures with local LM Studio backend · Issue #42270 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"feee315ff608b6fa\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/42270","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8602438aad9c23a8\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Reload](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/42270) to refresh your session.You signed out in another tab or window. *   [Sponsor](https://github.com/sponsors/openclaw). *   [Code](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw). *   [Issues 5k+](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues). *   [Pull requests 5k+](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pulls). *   [Security 368](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/security). *   [Code](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw). *   [Issues](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues). *   [Pull requests](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pulls). *   [Security](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/security). [[Bug]: OpenClaw 2026.3.8 regression: empty agent payloads + websocket 1006 closures with local LM Studio ba