otification settings. # Gateway dies after update and does not restart (regression in 2026.3.12) #44681. Gateway dies after update and does not restart (regression in 2026.3.12)#44681. ## Description. opened on Mar 13, 2026. ## Bug Report. **OS:** macOS 26.2 (arm64). ## Description. After running `openclaw update` to upgrade to 2026.3.12, the gateway process is killed but the LaunchAgent does not restart it automatically. The gateway dashboard becomes unreachable. This was previously reported and marked as self-resolved in 2026.3.8, but has regressed in 2026.3.12. ## Steps to Reproduce. 1. Run `openclaw update` (or let auto-update run). 2. Wait for update to complete. 3. Try to open the gateway dashboard → offline. 4. Gateway does not restart itself. ## Expected Behavior. Gateway restarts automatically after an update, as it did before 2026.3.8. ## Actual Behavior. ## Additional Notes. * `openclaw gateway restart` via the exec tool also exhibits this issue (kills gateway, doesn't restart it). * Workaround: manually run the launchctl command above. ## Metadata. ## Metadata. ### Assignees. ### Fields. No fields configured for issues without a type. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d6b6c1a346b296dd\">>>","score":0.9998969},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"35f4d7df44271b8d\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: Token usage shows as 'unknown' in 2026.3.7 (regression from 3.2) · Issue #39620 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"35f4d7df44271b8d\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/39773/linked_closing_reference?reference_location=REPO_ISSUES_INDEX","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9a5e91a5cfbe014f\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nToken usage information displays as \"unknown\" in session\\_status and openclaw sessions output after upgrading to OpenClaw 2026.3.7. usage payloads, so session history/status no longer regress to unknown token utilization for otherwise successful runs.\" This suggests a fix was attempted, but it appears to have introduced or not fully resolved the issue. Regression Testing2026.3.2: Token usage displays correctly2026.3.7: Token usage shows as \"unknown\" Impact Cannot monitor API costs during sessions Cannot track context window usage Difficult to manage token budget for long conversations WorkaroundDowngrade to OpenClaw 2026.3.2: pnpm remove -g openclawpnpm install -g openclaw@2026.3.2 Possible CausesContextEngine plugin interface changes in 3.7 may have broken usage reportingkimi-k2.5 model usage parsing may have regressed Status display formatting may not be reading usage data correctly despite API success Requested FixRestore token usage display in session_status and openclaw sessions output for 2026.3.7+. Token usage information displays as \"unknown\" in session\\_status and openclaw sessions output after upgrading to OpenClaw 2026.3.7. Token usage information displays as \"unknown\" in session\\_status and openclaw sessions output after upgrading to OpenClaw 2026.3.7.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9a5e91a5cfbe014f\">>>","score":0.99985576},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1022ee1d3d270132\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nUser-installed plugins cannot resolve `openclaw/plugin-sdk` module path (regression in 3.23) · Issue #53403 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1022ee1d3d270132\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/53403","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"65c784e8b6d4d1fe\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTitle: User-installed plugins cannot resolve `openclaw/plugin-sdk` module path (regression in 3.23) · Issue #53403 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n# Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. You signed out in another tab or window. You switched accounts on another tab or window. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # User-installed plugins cannot resolve `openclaw/plugin-sdk` module path (regression in 3.23) #53403. User-installed plugins cannot resolve `openclaw/plugin-sdk` module path (regression in 3.23)#53403. * OpenClaw 3.23 (ccfeecb) and 3.23-1. * macOS 15.7.4 x64. * Plugin: `@tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin` 1.0.2 / 1.0.3. * Plugin install path: `~/.openclaw/extensions/openclaw-weixin/`. 1. Install OpenClaw 3.23. 2. Install any user plugin that imports from `openclaw/plugin-sdk` (e.g. 3. 3. Start or restart the gateway 4. Plugin fails to load: `Error: Cannot find module 'openclaw/plugin-sdk'`. Bundled plugins (feishu, etc.) work fine — the issue only affects user-installed plugins in `~/.openclaw/extensions/`. ## Root Cause. In `pi-embedded-CwMQzdKD.js`, `loadOpenClawPlugins()` calls `buildPluginLoaderAliasMap(modulePath)` where `modulePath` is the plugin file path (e.g. `~/.openclaw/extensions/openclaw-weixin/index.ts`). The jiti-based loader uses this to build an alias map for `openclaw/plugin-sdk*` imports. The alias map builder has two resolution paths:. Finds `root-alias.cjs` by walking **up to 6 levels** from the plugin directory. For `~/.openclaw/extensions/openclaw-weixin/`:. 1. ~/.openclaw/extensions/openclaw-weixin/ 2. Never reaches `/usr/local/lib/node_modules/openclaw/` → returns `null`. Calls `resolveLoaderPluginSdkPackageRoot()` → `resolveOpenClawPackageRootSync()` starting from plugin dirname, then `findNearestPluginSdkPackageRoot()` (max 12 levels). Same problem — cannot reach the OpenClaw package root from `~/.openclaw/extensions/`. ### Why it worked in 3.13. In 3.13, the alias for `openclaw/plugin-sdk` (main entry only) used a different resolution strategy that could locate the OpenClaw package. In 3.23, both main entry and subpath resolution fail for user-installed plugins. Bundled plugins work because they are located at `/usr/local/lib/node_modules/openclaw/dist/extensions/` — inside the same package tree. 1. **Search the OpenClaw executable's location** as a candidate root in `resolveLoaderPluginSdkPackageRoot()`. 2. **Set `NODE_PATH`** to include the OpenClaw package parent in the gateway LaunchAgent. 3. **Add a config option** like `plugins.sdkPath` pointing to the OpenClaw installation directory. 4. **Extend the directory walk limit** or use `require.resolve()` to find the OpenClaw package from the gateway process itself. cc @X\\_Corperation (who reported the same issue in the community). ### Fields. No fields configured for issues without a type. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"65c784e8b6d4d1fe\">>>","score":0.99985456}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1775084677460}}
