 a Feishu channel using: `openclaw channels add --channel feishu --name default`. 3. Try to manually add a second Feishu channel or modify the agent configuration. ## Error Logs. Config warnings: - plugins.entries.feishu: plugin feishu: duplicate plugin id detected; later plugin may be overridden (/Users/maxhou/.openclaw/extensions/feishu/index.ts). The warning appears on every command, and Gateway becomes unstable when modifying channel configuration. ## Environment. * OpenClaw version: 2026.3.2. * OS: macOS 25.2.0 (arm64). * Feishu plugin: @openclaw/feishu@2026.3.1. ## Expected Behavior. Gateway should handle Feishu plugin gracefully without duplicate registration warnings, and modifying channel configuration should not cause crashes. ## Actual Behavior. 1. Duplicate plugin warning appears on every CLI command. * Manually editing openclaw.json to add channel bindings. * Adding multiple Feishu channel accounts. 3. The Feishu plugin is only installed once (confirmed via plugins.installs), but loaded twice by Gateway. ## Possible Root Cause. The Feishu plugin is being loaded twice during Gateway initialization, causing:. 1. Plugin ID conflict (duplicate detected). 2. Unstable behavior when modifying channel configurations. ## Additional Notes. * This affects the ability to bind different agents to different Feishu bots. * Workaround: Use terminal to manually start agents with `openclaw agent`  instead of channel-based routing. ## Metadata. ## Metadata. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"af042ec3bdbc4523\">>>","score":0.9999962},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"cedeb4051d95e4ed\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]:feishu plugin install issue · Issue #13448 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"cedeb4051d95e4ed\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/13448","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"371f4904