 * Cross-platform (WeCom -> Feishu) works correctly. ### Steps to reproduce. Configure both Feishu and WeCom channels. Set messages.tts.auto: \"always\". Send a message from Feishu. Reply is sent as TTS audio. Audio is truncated to only 2-3 words. ### Expected behavior. 2. Full TTS audio should be played. ### Actual behavior. 1. When using the Feishu channel, TTS audio is truncated when:. 2. * User sends message via Feishu. 3. * AI replies with TTS audio to Feishu. 4. * Only a few words are played (e.g., 2-3 words). ### OpenClaw version. 1. * OpenClaw version: 2026.2.26. ### Operating system. 操作系统：OpenCloudOS 版本号：9.4 内核版本：6.6.117-45.1.oc9.x86\\_64 类似于 CentOS 9 / RHEL 9. ### Install method. ### Logs, screenshots, and evidence. ### Impact and severity. ### Additional information. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't workingbug:behaviorIncorrect behavior without a crashIncorrect behavior without a crash. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0884f94c516c5bb6\">>>","score":0.99997556},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c60dd7146e62ced0\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: Feishu plugin still prompts to download after installation · Issue #39642 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c60dd7146e62ced0\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/39642","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"83577a7c653c0b88\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTitle: [Bug]: Feishu plugin still prompts to download after installation · Issue #39642 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. There was an error while loading. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # [Bug]: Feishu plugin still prompts to download after installation #39642. [[Bug]: Feishu plugin still prompts to download after installation](#top)#39642. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't workingbug:behaviorIncorrect behavior without a crashIncorrect behavior without a crash. ## Description. opened on Mar 8, 2026. ### Bug type. Behavior bug (incorrect output/state without crash). ### Summary. ### English. When adding a Feishu channel, the system prompts to download the Feishu plugin (@openclaw/feishu) for the first time. However, after downloading, the system still prompts that the plugin needs to be downloaded, even though the download has been completed. After that, it keeps prompting to download repeatedly. ### Simplified Chinese. ### Steps to reproduce. Skip operations such as configuration models. 1. Download and install the OpenClaw Feishu plugin (@openclaw/feishu). │ ● Download from npm (@openclaw/feishu) │ ○ Skip for now └. 1. Select a channel: ● Feishu/Lark (飞书) , Still showing download options：. │ ● Download from npm (@openclaw/feishu) │ ○ Skip for now └. ### Expected behavior. After downloading the plugin, it should work properly without repeatedly prompting to download. ### Actual behavior. Even though the plugin has been downloaded, the installation prompt still appears, preventing the addition of Feishu channel. ### OpenClaw version. ### Operating system. Debian GNU/Linux 13 (trixie). ### Install method. npm install -g openclaw@latest. ### Logs, screenshots, and evidence. ### Impact and severity. ### Additional information. ## Metadata. ## Metadata. ### Labels. bugSomething isn't workingSomething isn't workingbug:behaviorIncorrect behavior without a crashIncorrect behavior without a crash. ### Fields. No fields configured for issues without a type. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"83577a7c653c0b88\">>>","score":0.9999751},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c0dc5abf6bef2d42\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: Feishu Channel Fails to Send Replies Despite Successful Agent Processing · Issue #38686 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c0dc5abf6bef2d42\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/38686","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"86fb169ffe555d3d\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n# [Bug]: Feishu Channel Fails to Send Replies Despite Successful Agent Processing #38686. [[Bug]: Feishu Channel Fails to Send Replies Despite Successful Agent Processing](#top)#38686. My Feishu channel in OpenClaw is unable to send any replies back to the user. The system successfully receives messages from Feishu, dispatches them to the correct agent, and the agent processes the request and generates a response (visible in the OpenClaw dashboard and session files). `feishu[media-manager]: dispatch complete (queuedFinal=false, replies=0)`. 5. Observe that no reply is sent back to the user in Feishu. The root cause of this issue is a bug within the OpenClaw Feishu plugin's reply dispatch logic. The `reply-dispatcher` for the Feishu channel is incorrectly determining that there are no replies to send (`replies=0`), even when the agent has successfully generated a valid response. The fact that the WeCom channel works correctly suggests this is a channel-specific implementation bug, not a core OpenClaw framework issue.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"86fb169ffe555d3d\">>>","score":0.9999542},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f932999a86ad50a1\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: Config warnings:\\n- plugins.entries.feishu: plugin feishu: duplicate plugin id detected; later plugin may be overridden (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/openclaw/extensions/feishu/index.ts) · Issue #10287 · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f932999a86ad50a1\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/10287","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d20b19d74eb1c2a7\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n## Navigation Menu. # Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. * Notifications  You must be signed in to change notification settings. # [Bug]: Config warnings:\\n- plugins.entries.feishu: plugin feishu: duplicate plugin id detected; later plugin may be overridden (/usr/local/lib/node\\_modules/openclaw/extensions/feishu/index.ts) #10287. [[Bug]: Config warnings:\\n- plugins.entries.feishu: plugin feishu: duplicate plugin id detected; later plugin may be overridden (/usr/local/lib/node\\_modules/openclaw/extensions/feishu/index.ts)](#top)#10287. always :Config warnings:\\n- plugins.entries.feishu: plugin feishu: duplicate plugin id detected; later plugin may be overridden (/usr/local/lib/node\\_modules/openclaw/extensions/feishu/index.ts). ## Expected behavior. What did you expect to happen? ## Actual behavior. ## Logs or screenshots. Paste relevant logs or add screenshots (redact secrets). ### Fields. No fields configured for issues without a type. No branches or pull requests. ## Issue actions. You can’t perform that action at this time.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d20b19d74eb1c2a7\">>>","score":0.9999528}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1775084708201}}
