AL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0e673a30bc62c014\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.99805814\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e4469f22f6f7e2bb\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n[Bug]: #LosslessClaw + OpenClaw v2026.3.11: Tasks stop silently ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e4469f22f6f7e2bb\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/44511\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"42d40d96a592dd73\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nYou signed in with another tab or window. # [Bug]: #LosslessClaw + OpenClaw v2026.3.11: Tasks stop silently, token shows `n/a`, context compression not triggered #44511. [[Bug]: #LosslessClaw + OpenClaw v2026.3.11: Tasks stop silently, token shows `n/a`, context compression not triggered](#top)#44511. After upgrading to OpenClaw v2026.3.11 with LosslessClaw enabled, long tasks silently halt, session token displays  n/a , and context compression never triggers due to broken context engine interop. 4. Observe: task stops | token  n/a  | fallback/exports errors in log. Long-running tasks halt silently in the middle with no error message or reply posted. Affected: All users running OpenClaw v2026.3.11 with LosslessClaw enabled. Consequence: Long tasks stop silently without feedback; context compression fails; agent cannot finish jobs; no error visibility; manual  /reset  required to avoid interruption. Temporary workaround: Manually run  /compact  during long‑running tasks to force context compression and prevent silent termination. Additional context: This issue only occurs with LosslessClaw enabled, due to incompatible interception over the refactored context/token‑counting interface.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"42d40d96a592dd73\\\">>>\",\n      \"score\": 0.9975274\n    }\n  ]\n}"}],"details":{"query":"site:github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues \"plugin channel\" \"unknown channel\" openclaw","provider":"tavily","count":10,"tookMs":1947,"externalContent":{"untrusted":true,"source":"web_search","provider":"tavily","wrapped":true},"results":[{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3fcc09f0d99bb1a5\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: None of the channel plugins are working (2026-2-22.2) #24382\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3fcc09f0d99bb1a5\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/24382","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"54c3a8a9b229eb91\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n# Search code, repositories, users, issues, pull requests... You signed in with another tab or window. You signed out in another tab or window. You switched accounts on another tab or window. # [Bug]: None of the channel plugins are working (2026-2-22.2) #24382. [[Bug]: None of the channel plugins are working (2026-2-22.2)](#top)#24382. On a fresh install of the latest version of openclaw (2026-2-22.2) now of the channels configuration is working. openclaw configure shows all of the channels as plugin disabled. on running `openclaw plugins enable discord` it is success but nothing happens. the only way to fix it is to run `openclaw plugins install @openclaw/discord` which install a duplicate plug at ~/.openclaw/extenstions. 1. fresh install openclaw (2026-2-22.2) using install script. 2. configure telegram/discord channel. 3. it will say plugin disabled. ### Expected behavior. telegram, discord and otehr channels plugins should be enabled by default and working. ### Actual behavior. ### OpenClaw version. No fields configured for issues without a type. ## Issue actions.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"54c3a8a9b229eb91\">>>","score":0.99991584},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"cd8b6f17135a0a7d\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nPlugin install fails on Windows: spawn npm ENOENT #1963 - GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"cd8b6f17135a0a7d\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/1963","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"db6166391be46e63\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nDescription. Plugin installation via the web UI fails on Windows with: \\ Install failed (unknown exit): spawn npm ENOENT\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"db6166391be46e63\">>>","score":0.99918324},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"aecd7d4904846950\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nchannels.modelByChannel rejected by config validator as unknown ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"aecd7d4904846950\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/23084","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ad055965c9c73058\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThis prevents the gateway from starting with a valid modelByChannel configuration. Steps to Reproduce. Install openclaw@2026.2.21-2; Set\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ad055965c9c73058\">>>","score":0.99906737},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"403186112bc35f4e\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: [Windows] plugins install fails with spawn npm ENOENT #4557\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"403186112bc35f4e\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/4557","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"4de207d067e15cbd\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n# [Bug]: [Windows] plugins install fails with `spawn npm ENOENT` #4557. [[Bug]: [Windows] plugins install fails with `spawn npm ENOENT`](#top)#4557. On Windows, installing a plugin with `openclaw plugins install` fails with a `spawn npm ENOENT` error, even though Node.js and npm are correctly installed and available in PATH. The issue occurs in **both `cmd.exe` and PowerShell**, indicating this is not shell-specific but a Windows process spawning issue. 1. Install OpenClaw on Windows using the official installer:. Open a new terminal (cmd.exe or PowerShell). The plugin should be installed successfully using npm, assuming Node.js and npm are installed and vailable in the environment. The command fails with the following error in both cmd.exe and PowerShell:. [openclaw] Failed to start CLI: Error: spawn npm ENOENT at ChildProcess._handle.onexit (node:internal/child_process:285:19) With NODE_DEBUG=child_process enabled, OpenClaw is observed attempting to spawn npm directly. Install method: install.cmd / install.ps1 (official Windows installer). This suggests OpenClaw is spawning npm without handling Windows-specific behavior (e.g. using npm.cmd or enabling shell: true).\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"4de207d067e15cbd\">>>","score":0.99899167},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"7a9c35599af7eacd\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: Isolated OpenClaw browser (Brave) frequently becomes ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"7a9c35599af7eacd\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/10994","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0fb642b857372792\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nSummary. When Openclaw runs automated steps in the OpenClaw-managed isolated browser (Brave), the browser automation often stops mid-task.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0fb642b857372792\">>>","score":0.9989837},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"90f23ea5cfc8f87a\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: [summary / workaround] All plugins with `dependencies` can't ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"90f23ea5cfc8f87a\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/13913","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"dc0d6276f4f79bca\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nAll plugins with dependencies including: @openclaw/feishu; @openclaw/matrix; @openclaw/msteams; @openclaw/googlechat\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"dc0d6276f4f79bca\">>>","score":0.9989837},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e41e54225c652398\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[Bug]: Regression: All channel plugins disabled in v2026.2.22 ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e41e54225c652398\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/24395","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\